      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The above-entitled matter came on for oral argument before the Supreme Court of the United States at 11:09 a.m."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2017-17-432",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "20bb41799be72e142719dd0b36bf2f59ebbdea9e08c217c8ee74d6c0c0c039ff",
      "evidence_id": "ev-20bb41799be7-0000-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 5,
        "start": 5
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GINSBURG: Is it your position that once certification is denied, then members of the now-defunct class can come in and bring their own individual actions, but that's it?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2017-17-432",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "20bb41799be72e142719dd0b36bf2f59ebbdea9e08c217c8ee74d6c0c0c039ff",
      "evidence_id": "ev-20bb41799be7-0000-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 8,
        "start": 8
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: I'm sorry, that's not -- the statute doesn't talk about the best represent -- best representative in terms of individual members. It says the best representative is who has the greatest financial interest."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2017-17-432",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "20bb41799be72e142719dd0b36bf2f59ebbdea9e08c217c8ee74d6c0c0c039ff",
      "evidence_id": "ev-20bb41799be7-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 24,
        "start": 24
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "So, assuming Justice Kennedy's hypothetical, cases lasted more than the statute of limitations, there's a thousand individual suits that were filed, could the Court then say: Those thousand I'm going to treat as a class? You're saying no."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Aronson",
      "case_id": "2017-17-432",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "20bb41799be72e142719dd0b36bf2f59ebbdea9e08c217c8ee74d6c0c0c039ff",
      "evidence_id": "ev-20bb41799be7-0001-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 24,
        "start": 24
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "If it's a class of those thousand people only, I could see that the court might want to deal with that, but it doesn't have to be a class. The court can deal with it however it wants to."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Aronson",
      "case_id": "2017-17-432",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "20bb41799be72e142719dd0b36bf2f59ebbdea9e08c217c8ee74d6c0c0c039ff",
      "evidence_id": "ev-20bb41799be7-0001-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 25,
        "start": 25
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "certify a class of absent class members who have slept on their rights and are not entitled to tolling."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Gorsuch",
      "case_id": "2017-17-432",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "20bb41799be72e142719dd0b36bf2f59ebbdea9e08c217c8ee74d6c0c0c039ff",
      "evidence_id": "ev-20bb41799be7-0001-0006",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 36,
        "start": 36
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I'm sorry, and that's pretty unusual, right? I can't think of another example in equitable tolling doctrine where we do this, which may suggest some question about whether American Pipe is correct."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2017-17-432",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "20bb41799be72e142719dd0b36bf2f59ebbdea9e08c217c8ee74d6c0c0c039ff",
      "evidence_id": "ev-20bb41799be7-0001-0007",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 38,
        "start": 38
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Mr. Frederick, there's one thing I find very puzzling about your argument. That is your reliance on Shady Grove. Rule 23 says nothing about tolling."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2017-17-432",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "20bb41799be72e142719dd0b36bf2f59ebbdea9e08c217c8ee74d6c0c0c039ff",
      "evidence_id": "ev-20bb41799be7-0002-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 46,
        "start": 46
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Is that right?"
    },
    {
